-- title:
--   g⊗1-1⊗ g lies in the diagonal ideal
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, let $m$ be a natural number, and let $g$ be a polynomial in $R[x_0,\dots,x_{m-1}] =$ `MvPolynomial (Fin m) R`. The assertion is that there exists a family $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to R[x]\otimes_R R[x]$ of elements of the tensor product of the polynomial ring with itself over $R$ such that $$g\otimes 1 - 1\otimes g = \sum_{j} a_j\,\bigl(x_j\otimes 1 - 1\otimes x_j\bigr),$$ the sum being over all $j \in \mathrm{Fin}\,m$ and the products and differences being taken in the commutative ring $R[x]\otimes_R R[x]$ with its usual algebra structure. In other words, the element $g\otimes 1 - 1\otimes g$ belongs to the ideal of $R[x]\otimes_R R[x]$ generated by the $m$ elements $x_j\otimes 1 - 1\otimes x_j$, and the statement records a choice of coefficients witnessing this; no uniqueness is claimed.
--
--   This is the standard fact that the kernel of the multiplication map $R[x]\otimes_R R[x]\to R[x]$ — the diagonal ideal, whose square-zero quotient carries the module of Kähler differentials — is generated by the differences $x_j\otimes 1 - 1\otimes x_j$ coming from the variables, in the explicit form of Bézout-type coefficients for a given $g$. It is used in the construction of the dual basis and trace form attached to a square presentation, in [`Algebra.exists_dual_bijective_mul_and_trace_eq_jacobianDet_mul_of_square_presentation`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_dual_bijective_mul_and_trace_eq_jacobianDet_mul_of_square_presentation).
